Third-party material in this module
===================================

ByeDPI (https://github.com/hufrea/byedpi), MIT License, Copyright (c) 2024
hufrea. The license text is in BYEDPI-LICENSE. Derived from it:

- fake_payload.go: the default fake TLS ClientHello template (packets.c,
  v0.17.3), copied byte for byte.
- fake_windows.go: the TransmitFile mechanism of the Windows fake (send the
  prefix from a temporary file with a low TTL, rewrite the file with the
  original bytes for the retransmission), desync.c send_fake for _WIN32.
- fake_linux.go: the Linux fake mechanism (vmsplice a page holding the fake
  bytes into a pipe, splice it to the socket with a low TTL, wait until it was
  sent, overwrite the page with the original bytes, restore the TTL),
  desync.c send_fake and restore_state for __linux__. Reimplemented in Go;
  the mapping is MAP_SHARED instead of MAP_PRIVATE.
- disorder.go: the semantics of --disorder (hop limit 1 for a piece, restored
  before the next one), --oob and --disoob (the piece and one urgent byte sent
  with MSG_OOB), desync.c DESYNC_DISORDER, DESYNC_OOB, DESYNC_DISOOB and
  send_oob. Reimplemented in Go; the default urgent byte 'a' is ByeDPI's.
- fake_hello.go: the decoy ClientHello options --fake-sni (a list with one
  name drawn per connection; the wildcards '*', '?' and '#' of copy_name),
  --fake-tls-mod rand and orig (randomize_tls: random, session ID and key
  share values; the real ClientHello as the decoy base) and --fake-offset,
  packets.c change_tls_sni, randomize_tls, copy_name and desync.c
  get_tcp_fake. Reimplemented in Go by decoding and re-encoding the
  handshake instead of resizing it in place.
- conn.go: the fake as one of several split parts (the piece between the
  previous cut and the fake position is sent as fake, the pieces around it
  normally; Linux waits until earlier bytes were transmitted before lowering
  the hop limit), desync.c desync() with DESYNC_FAKE among other parts and
  sock_has_notsent.

zapret (https://github.com/bol-van/zapret), MIT License, Copyright (c)
2016-2024 bol-van. The license text is in ZAPRET-LICENSE. Derived from it:

- autottl.go: the hop count guess from a received TTL and the standard
  initial TTLs 64/128/255 within 32 hops (nfq/darkmagic.c hop_count_guess),
  and the delta/min/max TTL policy with the defaults 1, 3 and 20 and the
  rejection of a TTL not below the hop count (autottl_eval,
  AUTOTTL_DEFAULT_DESYNC_*, --dpi-desync-autottl), v72.13. Reimplemented in
  Go; 64 and 128 are read as zero hops.
